{"about_you":"Desk job in marketing. Currently deep in a stressful new project with lots of late nights, which is driving higher-calorie takeout (burritos, chips) and evening snacking. Strong self-tracker — 21-day logging streak even under pressure. Days tend to be built from 3 larger items that run carb/fat heavy and protein-light. Goal: 162 → 145 lb at a relaxed ~0.5 lb/week pace.","assessment":"Honest read: the plan said 1,550–1,700, but the last 6 logged days all landed **1,980–2,400 kcal** — consistently 300–700 over the ceiling. The trend weight reflects it: 158 lb, up ~0.4 lb/week instead of easing toward 145. This isn't a willpower problem — it lines up exactly with the stressful new project and late nights. The 21-day logging streak is the thing keeping this fixable: you're seeing it clearly, and that's the hard part.","calorie_max":1900,"calorie_min":1700,"changelog_note":"Raised range to 1,700–1,900 (from 1,550–1,700) — last 6 days ran ~2,200 avg and trend ticked up; set a realistic step-down instead of repeating a target reality blew past.","goal_summary":"Reach 145 lb at a relaxed pace","headline":"Let's reset the range — the last two weeks ran high","insights":[{"body":"Three weeks logging straight through a stressful project. That consistency is exactly why we can see the drift and course-correct. Don't lose this.","title":"21-day streak — this is the win","tone":"win"},{"body":"158 lb trending +0.4 lb/week. Six straight days at 1,980–2,400 is why. New 1,700–1,900 range is a realistic step back toward loss.","title":"Trend nudged up, not down","tone":"watch"},{"body":"Tonight's chips were 860 kcal / 37g fat and the day's biggest. Swapping that one item for something protein-based gets you back in range faster than cutting everything.","title":"The dinner item is the lever","tone":"nudge"},{"body":"80g today, 71–90g this week — under your 105g target most days. More protein, fewer calories, and you stay fuller through late nights.","title":"Protein still lagging","tone":"nudge"},{"body":"17 of 81 oz today. Low water often reads as hunger during late work sessions — easy extra bottle before the evening snack reach.","title":"Water's way behind","tone":"nudge"}],"protein_target":105,"strategy":"The gap between plan and reality is too wide to just repeat the old numbers. So we meet you where you are and tighten gradually instead of asking for a 500-cal cliff overnight.

**New range: 1,700–1,900 kcal.** That's a realistic step down from your recent ~2,200 average — enough to tip the trend back toward loss without white-knuckling during a busy stretch.

The pattern is clear: your days are built on 3 big items (burrito, chips, muffin+latte) that are carb/fat heavy and protein-light. The fix isn't eating *less often* — it's swapping the heaviest item. Today's 860-cal chips dinner is the single biggest lever. Protein's been drifting under target (75–90g) too — leaning protein-forward keeps you full on fewer calories.","timeframe":"relaxed pace, ~0.5 lb/week"}

{"about_you":"Software engineer on a lean-gain goal toward 172 lb. Started a new job with a long commute and tends to skip lunch, which is leaving him well under his calorie floor most days (~2,050–2,200 vs a 2,650 target). Trains consistently (~4 sessions/week) and is an excellent logger — 21-day streak. Responds to a clear, simple fix (add one meal) rather than overhauling existing meals.","assessment":"Training and logging are rock solid — **21-day streak** is excellent. But the scale is the tell: trend weight is **160 lb and drifting DOWN ~0.6 lb/week** when the plan is a lean *gain*. You're eating ~2,050–2,200 kcal most days, consistently **400–600 under the floor**. You can't build toward 172 while losing weight. This is fixable fast — it's a fueling gap, not an effort problem.","calorie_max":2850,"calorie_min":2650,"changelog_note":"Flagged off-track: trend dropped to 160 lb (-0.6 lb/wk) against a lean-gain goal; refocused insights on closing the ~500 kcal under-floor gap via a daily lunch. Range and protein held.","headline":"Off pace for 172 — eating's too low to grow","insights":[{"body":"Weight's drifting down 0.6 lb/week — but the goal is a lean GAIN. You're under the floor nearly every day. Add food, not restriction.","title":"Trend is going the wrong way","tone":"watch"},{"body":"Every day logs just 3 items. A ~550 kcal lunch (chicken wrap, rice bowl) closes almost the entire 400–600 kcal shortfall by itself.","title":"The missing lunch is the gap","tone":"nudge"},{"body":"Three straight weeks of logging, no gaps. This consistency is exactly what makes the fix easy — we can see precisely where to add.","title":"21-day streak","tone":"win"},{"body":"You've drifted from near-target to ~100g. A protein-forward lunch pulls you back toward 145 and supports the gain.","title":"Protein slipping to ~100g","tone":"nudge"},{"body":"Only ~5 bottles short of nothing — you're way behind by midday. Keep a bottle at your desk; it also helps appetite stay up.","title":"Water at 17 of 79 oz","tone":"nudge"}],"protein_target":145,"strategy":"The goal hasn't changed — a lean gain to 172 at ~0.5 lb/week. But you've been eating like someone cutting, not building.

**The fix: add one meal, don't white-knuckle bigger ones.** You're logging only 3 items a day — the missing lunch (new commute) is the whole gap. A real lunch of ~500–600 kcal puts you right in range.

I'm holding the range at **2,650–2,850** — that's what builds. The job isn't to eat perfectly, it's to stop landing under the floor. Protein's slipping a touch too (100g today vs 145 target) — a lunch with real protein fixes both at once."}
